Source: indi-stable-3rdparty-libs
Section: science
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Will Snyder <william@williamlsnyder.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               g++,
               indi-stable-core-dev,
               libusb-1.0-0-dev,
               libcurl4-gnutls-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/indilib/indi-3rdparty
Rules-Requires-Root: no

# Mirrors core/rpm/indi-stable-3rdparty-libs.spec -- same private prefix, same
# 9 bundled vendors, same licence-tier exclusions. Read that spec's header
# comment for the full rationale; not repeated here verbatim, only the
# Debian-specific mechanics (see core/deb-3rdparty-libs/rules).
#
# Every -dev package below Depends on its runtime sibling by NAME
# (= ${binary:Version}), not ${shlibs:Depends} -- deliberately, from the
# start, unlike core/rpm's own -devel subpackages, which had to add this
# after their first real `dnf install` failed with "nothing provides
# libapogee.so.3()(64bit)" (an auto-generated Requires on the -devel
# package's own unversioned .so symlink, unsatisfiable once
# __provides_exclude_from stripped the matching Provides). Debian's -dev
# convention of a hand-written package-name Depends, with no ${shlibs:Depends}
# on the -dev package at all, sidesteps that whole bug class by construction
# -- core/deb's own indi-stable-core-dev already does this, and it is the
# reason that packaging never hit the RPM-side defect.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-apogee
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Apogee Instruments CCD camera SDK (GPL-2.0)
 Apogee Instruments' CCD camera library, GPL-2.0 licensed -- source is
 included in this package's copyright file, satisfying GPL's own
 redistribution terms rather than merely permitting them.
 .
 Installs into /opt/indi-stable, the same private prefix as
 indi-stable-core, so it never collides with any distribution-provided
 camera SDK package.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party build. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the INDI project.

Package: indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-apogee-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-apogee (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Development files for indi-stable-3rdparty-libs-apogee
 Headers for building against the bundled Apogee SDK. Install path is
 /opt/indi-stable/include, matching indi-stable-core-dev's own headers --
 never under /usr/include, for the same reason core's headers are not there.

